  "term": "anterior cerebral artery",
  "definition": "The anterior cerebral artery is a blood vessel that branches from the internal carotid artery. Its branches supply parts of the brain including the caudate nucleus, internal capsule, putamen, septal nuclei, cingulate gyrus, and areas on the frontal and parietal lobes.",
